{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference","id":20943,"title":"Scions and Titan Spawn - What's the Difference?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-30T19:45:25-08:00","id":20943,"title":"Scions and Titan Spawn - What's the Difference?","content":"So for someone who hasn't got any of the books, but is interested in the game mechanics, is it possible to have a Scion who's parent was a titan?<br /> <br /> <br /> I ask, because I was thinking of making a Cthulhu Scion, but according to the website I looked up, The Great Old Ones are classified as Titans (yet calls them gods, oddly enough).<br /> <br /> <br /> I was thinking it might be possible if a Titan Spawn / Scion decided to switch sides and work for the other team if they might be considered one or the other. I've already read a couple notes around here saying how some gods choose to 'adopt' scions, rather than actually sire them, and wondered if that could apply to children of the opposing factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-30-2013, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T20:57:45-08:00","id":20976,"title":"","content":"Well, the children of titans are Titanspawn and the children of deities are Scions. It is possible for the Titanspawn to switch sides and work with the gods. I have an NPC who is like that. He is a rakshasa who was adopted by Vishnu. The same can be said of the reverse with a Greater Titan taking in a Scion since all it takes is a deity to renounce his ties to the Scion.<br /> <br /> The only real debate is if your gaming group allows Cthulhu as a Titan or as a deity. If he/she/it is a deity, then you can have a Scion. If they are Titans, then you would be playing a Titanspawn that could be adopted by a god to help in the war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T21:15:38-08:00","id":20981,"title":"","content":"Well is there any actual difference between them: Appearances, Capabilities, Equipment? As in do Titan Spawn also go from Hero, to Demi, to Full, or do they have a completely different stage of advancement?<br /> <br /> <br /> Or are they both pretty much the same thing, just from different parents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T22:42:18-08:00","id":21004,"title":"","content":"There are no three stages of advancement for Titanspawn. Not unless you want them to be for your creation. Titanspawn just show up with their power. They start (and end) with the power to turn people to stone or to burst into flame or to cause a brain aneurysm by smacking their chewing gum. They do not usually gain power.<br /> <br /> Again, this is the general principle but you can change it as suits your whim as an ST or else by working with your ST to come up with something homebrewed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T23:36:44-08:00","id":21022,"title":"","content":"A Titan can be the patron of an acknowledged Scion. That's usually when they go evil. A titan spawn adopted by a god can work but often has complications. It was also posited in Scion: God that Titan avatars can produce dark scions. They don't go into too much detail though. The big issue would be the virtues however. Either they would have titan virtues or they would have the virtues of the pantheon that the titan avatar is most closely associated with. It also depends on how closely they are related to mortals and what the titan wants them for. The Shinobi for instance serve the Titan of Darkness but have Amatsu-kami virtues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:56:57-08:00","id":21728,"title":"","content":"The sidebars you are looking at in God on pg 206 and 209 do indeed mention titanspawn scions or Dark scions. It presents them as an optional ploy by the titans to create servitors that are as powerful and mobile as those of the gods. The only details you get are that they; A) don't get birthrights (instead using titanspawn trophies as relics, with nothing about guides or followers mentioned), B) get slapped with some unusual twist (which I interpreted as physical mutation or quirk) whenever they learn boons, and C) can upgrade their legend whenever they want by replacing a previous virtue with a dark virtue. It can also be extrapolated that they D) have no PSP.<br /> <br /> I actually played one in a home game, the character ended up working for his titan, but since that titan was one of the handful of indifferent/neutral ones he was allowed to cooperate with godly scions against that titan's rivals/enemies/annoyances.<br /> <br /> Another detail they never get into is what a scion of an allied titan would be like. Examples of allied titans: Helios, Thanatos, Hypnos (who apparently crashes in Hades's underworld), Rhea (Zeus's mom), Chronos, Oceanus (whose daughter married Poseidon). These are titans who never got slapped into tarterus because they aren't titan-avatars, but they ARE titans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T15:18:23-08:00","id":21921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=21728#post21728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another detail they never get into is what a scion of an allied titan would be like. Examples of allied titans: Helios, Thanatos, Hypnos (who apparently crashes in Hades's underworld), Rhea (Zeus's mom), Chronos, Oceanus (whose daughter married Poseidon). These are titans who never got slapped into tarterus because they aren't titan-avatars, but they ARE titans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where is this? I'm interested in reading more of this.<br /> <br /> The only Greater Titans that weren't imprisoned were Logos, Greater Titan of Order (who sided with the Gods on the Titan War), Hundun, Greater Titan of Chaos (who doesn't have Avatars to imprison) and Vritra, Greater Titan of Drought (who was deeply wounded and regenerated deep on the Earth, don't ask, I also don't quite understand it).<br /> <br /> So note that all Gods are the decedents of the Greater Titans or from their Avatars, so there is no problem with the daughter of Oceanus marrying Poseidon. I also was under the impression that Helios was killed and absorbed by Aten, but I might be mistaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T17:27:34-08:00","id":21988,"title":"","content":"Where is Logos mentioned? I remember Hundun being mentioned in Scion: Companion and I would need to relook up Vitra. Wait, isn't Logos a fan Titan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T17:31:14-08:00","id":21990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=21988#post21988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is Logos mentioned? I remember Hundun being mentioned in Scion: Companion and I would need to relook up Vitra. Wait, isn't Logos a fan Titan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, but don't get your hopes up, this is all we know:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scion: God, page 153</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other Titans of such concepts as Love, Fear, Death, Time and more exist. Facets of them exist in other Titans (Fear exists in Darkness and Love exists in the World, for example), but some are large enough to demand their own entities. One or two Titans even remained free. For example, Logos, the primordial embodiment of order and justice, was never imprisoned. Her avatars Themis, Syn and Ma\u2019at accepted limitations to their power and disappeared into the background behind the Dodekatheon, the Aesir and the Pesedjet. Others are left to open to be personalized for your game, perhaps to threaten pantheons of your creation.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T17:33:34-08:00","id":21991,"title":"","content":"In one game I ran the NPC and later member of the group was a scion of Mikaboshi. Due to his closer mortal ties and growing his power himself rather than accept the boost from his father, he ended up having Amatsu Kami virtues. Later he would have been accepted as a member of the Amatsu-kami sue to his actions and the patronage of Tsuki-yomi.<br /> <br /> Oh, as far as PSPs that would be determined by the titan Avatar who is the parent. Each of the pantheon specific Titan Avatars also has the that pantheon's PSP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T00:30:30-08:00","id":22176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=21921#post21921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where is this? I'm interested in reading more of this.<br /> <br /> The only Greater Titans that weren't imprisoned were Logos, Greater Titan of Order (who sided with the Gods on the Titan War), Hundun, Greater Titan of Chaos (who doesn't have Avatars to imprison) and Vritra, Greater Titan of Drought (who was deeply wounded and regenerated deep on the Earth, don't ask, I also don't quite understand it).<br /> <br /> So note that all Gods are the decedents of the Greater Titans or from their Avatars, so there is no problem with the daughter of Oceanus marrying Poseidon. I also was under the impression that Helios was killed and absorbed by Aten, but I might be mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Logos, Hundun, and Vritra aren't the sole exceptions, they're examples. It is dismissively written in God that one or two overtitans were not imprisoned, but there clearly must be a lot more than that. It's not explicitly detailed anywhere, I just saw this as a glaring inconsistency left over from their description of titans and overtitans, as well as leaving out more obvious players of actual myth. I mean look at these holes; <br /> <br /> -Apollo doesn't drive the sun chariot full-time, Helios does, and Helios is a titan. They make vague mention that Aten might have diablerized (for lack of a better word) Hyperion, but Helios has been working for Zeus ever since the 1st titanomachy driving the sun chariot. He even had a scion after he started work called Phaeton in actual myth.<br /> -Oceanus is the original greek titan of the endless ocean, and the husband of Tethys, why would he NOT be in the drowned road, and where else would he go if he's not listed as an avatar? Nobody ever killed him in the actual myths, and they certainly never mention such happening in God, so he just retired or something and went away...but to WHERE? <br /> -Artemis is <i>associated</i> with the moon yes, but Selene IS the moon, and she isn't even mentioned even though she too is a benign titan (of Hyperion in fact) that lots of people actually know of. She had some affair with a human guy called Endymion whom she sent to sleep forever so he'd never get old and she could always have him.<br /> -I mentioned Rhea, who would logicaly appear in the titanrealm of Terra, as she too was a earth/fertility being, but she's nowhere to be found. And she sheltered Zeus from his father Kronos, I can't see her being thrown into tarterus either, when she was instrumental to the rise of the dodecatheon as we know it. The greeks may act like dicks but (like the Lanisters) they always pay their debts.<br /> -Zurvan's sole avatar is Ahriman (who actually has more in common with Darkness and Chaos than Time), but Chronos has ALWAYS been the controller of time. The universe begins in greek myth with Chronos and Ananke, but he is never mentioned EVER. If Ahriman is the sole avatar of Zurvan, when did he dispose of Chronos or where did Chronos go?<br /> -They punked Erebus when they slapped Mikaboshi (actually a star-god) into the realm of darkness, but he and Nyx were major powers on the level of Chronos, Ananke, Gaia, and Oranus eons before Kronos and that generation of titans were ever born. His children by Nyx are all the death, sleep, and light titans believe it or not, NONE of which are mentioned anywhere else in the material unless you go delving into the french supplements we didn't get. Then you hear mention of Morpheus (a god) child of Hypnos (a titan) when you read about the Key of Morpheus.<br /> <br /> What I deduced from all this that A) you can be a titan and NOT an avatar, and still not be a god; or B) more than just Logos sided with the gods, Hypnos (sleep), and Thanatos (death), must have done so as well; or C) an allied titan-avatar can go into some kind of refugee status and leave the titanrealm, escaping its fate but not specifically becoming a god in the process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T04:33:22-08:00","id":22255,"title":"","content":"I used Oceanus as a fill-in for Poseidon (who was killed in thr 1st Titanomachy). One player spent most of the Demigod cycle trying to find out which of the dodekatheon was a 'fake' - only to find out that it was the parent of the other greek scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T04:59:14-08:00","id":22268,"title":"","content":"I believe that you are mistakingly confusing the Scion Myth with Real Life Myth. While the first draws from the second in many ways, it isn't a copy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22176#post22176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Logos, Hundun, and Vritra aren't the sole exceptions, they're examples. It is dismissively written in God that one or two overtitans were not imprisoned, but there clearly must be a lot more than that. It's not explicitly detailed anywhere, I just saw this as a glaring inconsistency left over from their description of titans and overtitans, as well as leaving out more obvious players of actual myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do not that there are (or should be) an amount of Greater Titans equal to the amount of Pantheons and that we don't have all the Pantheons that exist, that is why many of us continue to write Pantheons. In this Forum there is someone trying to write a Holiday Pantheon, there is someone using the Great Old Ones as a Pantheons... they also have their opposing Greater Titan.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22176#post22176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Apollo doesn't drive the sun chariot full-time, Helios does, and Helios is a titan. They make vague mention that Aten might have diablerized (for lack of a better word) Hyperion, but Helios has been working for Zeus ever since the 1st titanomachy driving the sun chariot. He even had a scion after he started work called Phaeton in actual myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Aten is the only living Avatar of the Greater Titan of Light, Helios either has:<br /> a) Become a God, like Ged did. It isn't that uncommon, even the other way around.<br /> b) Was absorbed into Aten.<br /> c) Was forgiven by the gods, released from his Greater Titan allowed to serve the Dodekatheon.<br /> <br /> You can have whatever option in your games because it is open to interpretation.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22176#post22176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Oceanus is the original greek titan of the endless ocean, and the husband of Tethys, why would he NOT be in the drowned road, and where else would he go if he's not listed as an avatar? Nobody ever killed him in the actual myths, and they certainly never mention such happening in God, so he just retired or something and went away...but to WHERE?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he is in the Drowned Road, but he is so minor that he doesn't really matter much as opposition. Oceanus was a fairly good Titan in real myth.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22176#post22176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Artemis is <i>associated</i> with the moon yes, but Selene IS the moon, and she isn't even mentioned even though she too is a benign titan (of Hyperion in fact) that lots of people actually know of. She had some affair with a human guy called Endymion whom she sent to sleep forever so he'd never get old and she could always have him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe she is in the Greater Titan of Night, being the Moon there.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22176#post22176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-I mentioned Rhea, who would logicaly appear in the titanrealm of Terra, as she too was a earth/fertility being, but she's nowhere to be found. And she sheltered Zeus from his father Kronos, I can't see her being thrown into tarterus either, when she was instrumental to the rise of the dodecatheon as we know it. The greeks may act like dicks but (like the Lanisters) they always pay their debts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do believe that Rhea wasn't imprisoned, but she has either become a Goddess or released from her Greater Titan. But do note that Gaia was also very important to the rise of the Dodekatheon, but was also imprisioned.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22176#post22176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Zurvan's sole avatar is Ahriman (who actually has more in common with Darkness and Chaos than Time), but Chronos has ALWAYS been the controller of time. The universe begins in greek myth with Chronos and Ananke, but he is never mentioned EVER. If Ahriman is the sole avatar of Zurvan, when did he dispose of Chronos or where did Chronos go?</div> </div> </div> </div>While I might like Zrvan as a Titan of Time, I believe that they forced the Persian myths too much into the mold, while it would be better to break it. Basically, it is an example of a bad Greater Titan, even worse than Vritra in my opinion.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22176#post22176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-They punked Erebus when they slapped Mikaboshi (actually a star-god) into the realm of darkness, but he and Nyx were major powers on the level of Chronos, Ananke, Gaia, and Oranus eons before Kronos and that generation of titans were ever born. His children by Nyx are all the death, sleep, and light titans believe it or not, NONE of which are mentioned anywhere else in the material unless you go delving into the french supplements we didn't get. Then you hear mention of Morpheus (a god) child of Hypnos (a titan) when you read about the Key of Morpheus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, Scion Myth =/= Real Myth. I believe the place for Nyx is the Greater Titan of Stars or Night, since she isn't darkness, but the starry night sky.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22176#post22176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I deduced from all this that A) you can be a titan and NOT an avatar, and still not be a god; or B) more than just Logos sided with the gods, Hypnos (sleep), and Thanatos (death), must have done so as well; or C) an allied titan-avatar can go into some kind of refugee status and leave the titanrealm, escaping its fate but not specifically becoming a god in the process.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these are valid choices if you want to make them, but they aren't the Scion Myth Canon.<br /> <br /> Also, speak with Griffinguy24 about how badly are the Aztecs represented in Scion in comparison to real Mythology. Scion uses a mold that is the easiest understandable to the Western audience, the Greek Myths, so many things that real myth has no problem with in Scion it is a problem. Even the Greeks don't have Greater Titans that generate the Titans and the Gods; they make the distinctions as the Titans are the generation of beings before the beings the Greek worship, some of which were imprisoned because they were dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://s56.photobucket.com/user/Solkannar/media/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif.html\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i56.photobucket.com/albums/g165/Solkannar/assinatura-Man-in-Black-mas.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/384-man-in-black","name":"Man in Black","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar384_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T06:39:30-08:00","id":22307,"title":"","content":"I think there are a couple things that need to be repeated:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22268#post22268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that you are mistakingly confusing the Scion Myth with Real Life Myth. While the first draws from the second in many ways, it isn't a copy.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Man in Black</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=22268#post22268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, Scion Myth =/= Real Myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been tempted at time to rewrite a few things that put some of the gods on the opposing team, while the Titans were the good guys.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T11:10:50-08:00","id":22450,"title":"","content":"I wasn't confusing the two, my point is that with this wealth of info they could have done it this way in the first place with less effort than it took to cram stuff. I'm well aware they shoehorned most of this stuff together without much research. You mentioned the overtitan of Night which isn't canon either, just another example of what could have been fixed.<br /> <br /> However, we seem to have left topic. The question was whether a scion can have a titan parent, and depending on the terminology you use (in Helios or Rhea's case), or which sidebars you pay attention to, the answer is in fact YES.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/765-darksol-aeternium","name":"Darksol-aeternium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"392"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T15:30:56-08:00","id":22642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference#post20943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking it might be possible if a Titan Spawn / Scion decided to switch sides and work for the other team if they might be considered one or the other. I've already read a couple notes around here saying how some gods choose to 'adopt' scions, rather than actually sire them, and wondered if that could apply to children of the opposing factions.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are mythical precedents for a Titanspawn working for a God. Cerberus for instance.<br /> <br /> However, it should be noted the main difference between Scions and Titanspawn are the latter tend to be more overtly <i>monstrous.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T01:05:06-08:00","id":23006,"title":"","content":"It is interesting enough that books often mention that titanspawn are bound by the will of their masters, and also give examples of how to circumvent it. When Ymir died, frost giants and dwarves gained freedom; <i>Ragnarok</i> makes a whole paragraph on the subject of &quot;how titanspawn can switch allegiance&quot;.<br /> It makes me wonder - what if titanspawn were present in the World, but Titan influence was completely cut from them. Will they act according to Titans' will, or according to their own?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I must - so I can.<br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif\">Learning makes life more rewarding and enjoyable;...the worst thing of all is ignorance</span>.</i> <div align=\"right\">Alfred the Great</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1425-vi-zet","name":"Vi-Zet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T11:51:45-08:00","id":23250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vi-Zet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=23006#post23006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is interesting enough that books often mention that titanspawn are bound by the will of their masters, and also give examples of how to circumvent it. When Ymir died, frost giants and dwarves gained freedom; <i>Ragnarok</i> makes a whole paragraph on the subject of &quot;how titanspawn can switch allegiance&quot;.<br /> It makes me wonder - what if titanspawn were present in the World, but Titan influence was completely cut from them. Will they act according to Titans' will, or according to their own?</div> </div> </div> </div>probably depends on a case-specific basis. Some will strike out on their own, some will continue to try to carry out the will of the Titans, in the hopes that they'll come back, some may just kinda freeze up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T12:37:25-08:00","id":23268,"title":"","content":"Based on how the Titanspawn behaved when the Titans were imprisoned, it seems that a lot of them would just find somewhere quiet and go to sleep, waiting for the rumoured day when their masters returned...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Remember - popcorn can feel pain.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1195-frivyeti","name":"FrivYeti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T14:19:40-08:00","id":31216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksol-aeternium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=21728#post21728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sidebars you are looking at in God on pg 206 and 209 do indeed mention titanspawn scions or Dark scions. It presents them as an optional ploy by the titans to create servitors that are as powerful and mobile as those of the gods. The only details you get are that they; A) don't get birthrights (instead using titanspawn trophies as relics, with nothing about guides or followers mentioned), B) get slapped with some unusual twist (which I interpreted as physical mutation or quirk) whenever they learn boons, and C) can upgrade their legend whenever they want by replacing a previous virtue with a dark virtue. It can also be extrapolated that they D) have no PSP.<br /> <br /> I actually played one in a home game, the character ended up working for his titan, but since that titan was one of the handful of indifferent/neutral ones he was allowed to cooperate with godly scions against that titan's rivals/enemies/annoyances.<br /> <br /> Another detail they never get into is what a scion of an allied titan would be like. Examples of allied titans: Helios, Thanatos, Hypnos (who apparently crashes in Hades's underworld), Rhea (Zeus's mom), Chronos, Oceanus (whose daughter married Poseidon). These are titans who never got slapped into tarterus because they aren't titan-avatars, but they ARE titans.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;sidebar&quot; only mentions an accidental visitation by a Titan, it makes me wonder if an abandoned titanspawn adopted by a god would pattern after the god and progress normally, be forced to progress as titanspawn only, or if it would always be some kind of hybrid.<br /> <br /> <br /> In another game system I had a centaur Nightbane that I never really got to play (the GM only did the lead in scenario and abandoned the campaign for another one) and I am curious if a sion with some centaur blood and maybe a dark side that had to be resisted would work in Sion without distorting the background of the game to accommodate it. I was thinking of the character starting out as the usual human scion in form and taking on more centaur traits as she gains power and probably having a device (relic or boon or whatever is appropriate) to (at least eventually if it is not possible at Hero level) toggle between four and six limbs (or seven if the tail would be considered a limb...) and the &quot;base form&quot; eventually switching from human to centaur. The suspicion the character might be saddled with having been originally titanspawn-scion would fit in with the slightly pariah air that a Nightbane normally has.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","user":"BC001","date":". 12-16-2013, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T07:00:50-08:00","id":31630,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=31216#post31216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In another game system I had a centaur Nightbane that I never really got to play (the GM only did the lead in scenario and abandoned the campaign for another one) and I am curious if a sion with some centaur blood and maybe a dark side that had to be resisted would work in Sion without distorting the background of the game to accommodate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nightbane...hmm...Palladium stuff is pretty awesome. Very different though.<br /> From a myth point, the centaurs were a pretty brutish lot, with the sole exception being Chiron, whom I would think may have had his struggles with a &quot;dark side&quot; influence of his brethren.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BC001</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/20943-scions-and-titan-spawn-what-s-the-difference?p=31216#post31216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking of the character starting out as the usual human scion in form and taking on more centaur traits as she gains power and probably having a device (relic or boon or whatever is appropriate) to (at least eventually if it is not possible at Hero level) toggle between four and six limbs (or seven if the tail would be considered a limb...) and the &quot;base form&quot; eventually switching from human to centaur. The suspicion the character might be saddled with having been originally titanspawn-scion would fit in with the slightly pariah air that a Nightbane normally has.</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost sounds like the Nephilim game that came out way back when by Chaosium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T15:45:43-08:00","id":38465,"title":"","content":"I've always had difficulty in believing that the &quot;bad guys&quot; are evil for evil's sake. So I find perspectives and points of view from any side to be of interest.<br /> <br /> For example, the following is a bit paraphrased from John C. Wright's &quot;Titans of Chaos&quot;<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>We stood on the Plains of Vigrid, where the brink of Chaos roared, and the Gates of the World's End had been torn from their hinges, and lay stretched for miles along the plain.<br /> To one side reared all the armies of a united Chaos: a fearsome sight. I saw phantasmagorical dream-legions from outer realms of eternal night, sons of Morpheus and Nepenthe; I saw fallen spirits from the Abyss, armed and armored with incontestable magic; above them and below, a hundred miles or more in length, the soulless monsters from the Void, with all their engines and molecular alchemies of matter and energy; above and beyond them, nigh impossible to see or to imagine were creatures too perfect to be threatened or deterred; the uncreated thousand dimensional superbeings from the unthinkable primordial prereality, before the geometry of space-time was drawn. A sight to stir the soul, to look upon those beings, some brilliant with the splendor of eternal night; some wretched and lightning-scarred, yet smoldering with the burned remnants of angelic majesty; others yet with no souls at all, implacable and cold; others far too strange and wondrous ever to be allowed inside a sane universe, too large by far for space itself to hold..</i><br /> ...end snippet</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The character doing the talking is Boreas, and obviously on the Olympians' side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 12-28-2013, 06:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T07:12:32-08:00","id":41693,"title":"","content":"It's not a hard-and-fast distinction, and it probably shouldn't be. The gods are themselves a particular type of Titanspawn if you take the word literally, which means Scions are also Titanspawn in a sense. It's just the the word is normally used to designate beings that were born of the Titans that <i>aren't</i> on the side of the gods. They're monstrous or inimical to the order of the cosmos or otherwise hostile to gods and their Scions, so they get stuck with the Othering term. They're the black sheep of the family, so to speak (but family nonetheless).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-03T07:53:11-08:00","id":41711,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but it's the winners that make certain their version of history is the &quot;truth:&quot;<br /> <br /> Of from the titan perspective:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><i>&quot;My father is Achelous, the son of Oceanus, eldest son of Uranus. Oceanus is one of those who, for the sake of pity, entered this world to battle the grim Demiurge. He was deceived by the nature of time, and did not know what it was he was entering. It took him fifteen billion years to cross the Pontic Ocean of 'false vacuum' surrounding this reality; by the time he reached here, Saturn was overcome, replaced by children, the Olympians, who were far worse than Saturn ever had been.<br /> If Milton's Satan in Paradise Lost at least remembers what bright virtue he once had, and regrets its loss, imagine how much worse sons of Satan would be, raised from birth in the inferno. They would be devils softened by no living memory of Heaven.</i></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":".  spacing 01-03-2014, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}